From 99ccb3ab4861857bae041069aabd4931bfde93f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:55:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: MGMT: leave room for cnt events in the mesh done
 deadline

mesh_send_start_complete() arms the done work cnt * 25 ms after a mesh
packet was started. mesh_send_sync() adds the packet's advertising
instance with the adapter's advertising interval, 0x0800 (1280 ms)
unless userspace configured another one, and the controller sends the
first advertising event on enable and each further one an interval
later. With the default interval only the first of cnt events fits into
the deadline. doc/mgmt-protocol.rst defines Count as "the number of
times this packet will be sent before transmission completes".

So far the deadline did not limit what was sent, because nothing tore
the instance down when it expired. Once the done work removes the mesh
instance, a Count above 1 yields a single advertising event at the
default interval.

Arm the done work so that cnt events fit: the first at the start, each
further one an interval plus the up to 10 ms of advDelay later, and
25 ms after the last. A cnt of 1, which is what bluetooth-meshd sends
(it times its own retransmissions), keeps the 25 ms it has today, at
any interval. With an interval shorter than those 25 ms the controller
can still send one event more than cnt, as it does today.

Fixes: b338d91703fa ("Bluetooth: Implement support for Mesh")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/mgmt.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index b19ab17ff1b3..ca11195d8ba5 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -2343,9 +2343,18 @@ static void mesh_send_start_complete(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data, int err)
 		return;
 	}
 
-	mesh_send_interval = msecs_to_jiffies((send->cnt) * 25);
+	/* The instance was added with the adapter's advertising interval:
+	 * the first event is sent on enable, each further one an interval
+	 * plus up to 10 ms of advDelay later. Leave room for cnt events and
+	 * 25 ms after the last one, which is all a cnt of 1 gets.
+	 */
+	mesh_send_interval = 25;
+	if (send->cnt > 1)
+		mesh_send_interval += (send->cnt - 1) *
+			(INTERVAL_TO_MS(hdev->le_adv_max_interval) + 10);
+
 	queue_delayed_work(hdev->req_workqueue, &hdev->mesh_send_done,
-			   mesh_send_interval);
+			   msecs_to_jiffies(mesh_send_interval));
 }
 
 static int mesh_send_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data)

